<article class="env-lemma" id="060S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/060S">Lemma <span data-tag="060S">66.31.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ Y$-module. If $\mathcal{G}$ is locally projective on $Y$, then $f^*\mathcal{G}$ is locally projective on $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a surjective étale morphism $V \to Y$ with $V$ a scheme. Choose a surjective étale morphism $U \to V \times _ Y X$ with $U$ a scheme. Denote $\psi : U \to V$ the induced morphism. Then 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  f^*\mathcal{G}|_ U = \psi ^*(\mathcal{G}|_ V)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Hence the lemma follows from the definition and the result in the case of schemes, see Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/060M" data-tag="060M">28.22.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>